{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793382422487594001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"icebound-musicianly-parakeet","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"7a5310ca093f07fd4f3af33ff9b1aedeec4037c5baeac9dcb453883a1565bb42","event_uuid":"19f23a7f-ab12-478a-88ff-92a9907dac62","position":{"commit_sha":"54573d3064cd46c2e04d454d35ddc91429332d9c","position":"1793380111545539625-19f23a7f-ab12-478a-88ff-92a9907dac62"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"bf9e671fbdf8816881fbfe64df035879b24fbc5189999746ddde96ce80627bb8","event_uuid":"4b145231-129a-4ea7-bb10-046e4e118fe4","position":{"commit_sha":"1ad841e19a933d23cccf987574adc3899a23ae31","position":"1793380117740769862-4b145231-129a-4ea7-bb10-046e4e118fe4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793380111545539625,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4b145231-129a-4ea7-bb10-046e4e118fe4","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"19ba-bd62-1adb-41df"}],"description":"## Problem\n\n`docs/event-schema.md:256` locates `_clear_claimed_session` in `_processors.py`:\n\n```\n_processors.py _clear_claimed_session\n```\n\nThat is wrong on `origin/main` at `50d5a36539d`. The symbol is defined at\n`src/rebar/reducer/_processors_status.py:35` and is not imported into, re-exported from,\nor referenced by `_processors.py` at all — `git grep -nF '_clear_claimed_session'\nsrc/rebar/reducer/_processors.py` returns nothing.\n\nA reader following the locator opens the wrong module and finds no such symbol.\n\n## How it was found\n\nWhile censusing `_processors.py`'s re-exports for `censurable-exotic-snake`. Two\nneighbouring locators in the same file (`:234` `process_status`, `:249`\n`_fold_claimed_session`) are correct today and break when that story deletes the\nre-exports, so that story repairs them. This one is independent: it is wrong now and\nstays wrong whether or not that story lands, which is why it is tracked separately\nrather than folded in.\n\n## Change\n\nRewrite `:256` to `reducer/_processors_status.py:_clear_claimed_session`, matching the\nform already used at `:82` (`reducer/_processors_status.py:_fold_close_metadata`).\n\nThen sweep the rest of the file for the same defect class rather than fixing only the\none line: every `path:symbol` or `path symbol` locator in `docs/event-schema.md` is\nresolved against the tree, and any other locator naming a module that does not define or\nimport the symbol is corrected the same way.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] **AC1** `grep -cF '_processors.py _clear_claimed_session' docs/event-schema.md`\n      prints 0.\n- [ ] **AC2** `grep -cF 'reducer/_processors_status.py:_clear_claimed_session' docs/event-schema.md`\n      prints 1.\n- [ ] **AC3** Every locator in `docs/event-schema.md` naming a `reducer/` module and a\n      symbol resolves: for each, the named module defines or imports the named symbol,\n      verified by reading the module rather than by string match. The check is recorded\n      in a ticket comment listing each locator and its outcome.\n- [ ] **AC4** `git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD` lists exactly\n      `docs/event-schema.md`.\n- [ ] **AC5** `make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Out of scope — checked, not merely unexamined\n\n- `docs/event-schema.md:234` and `:249`, which are correct today and are repaired by\n  `censurable-exotic-snake` as part of the move that breaks them. If that story lands\n  first this ticket inherits a file where they are already fixed, and AC3 still covers\n  them.\n- Any change to the reducer modules themselves. This is a documentation-only fix.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d725-7f05-88fb-4e4a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Fix the stale _clear_claimed_session locator in docs/event-schema.md","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["19f23a7f-ab12-478a-88ff-92a9907dac62","4b145231-129a-4ea7-bb10-046e4e118fe4"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793382422487594001,"uuid":"9ee0e77c-b5ef-4c5c-86a9-1ecfe45d2117"}